    "taxonId": 76746,
    "summary": "An annual or short-lived perennial herb native to the Americas, Mexican tea has irregular branches, long narrow leaves and small green flowers. Its strongly aromatic leaves are used as a vegetable, seasoning and herbal tea, but overdoses of its essential oil have caused deaths.",
    "humanEdibility": "yes",
    "edibilityNote": "Leaves, preferably collected before seeding, are used as a vegetable, seasoning and herbal tea; the concentrated essential oil can be fatal.",
