    "taxonId": 322492,
    "summary": "An evergreen flowering perennial native to tropical and southern Africa, the spider plant has long narrow leaves and fleshy, tuberous roots. Its arching flowering stems carry plantlets that droop, touch soil and form roots. The roots are reportedly edible, although preparation is unstated and mild laxative effects are claimed.",
    "humanEdibility": "yes",
    "edibilityNote": "Tuberous roots are reportedly edible, with raw or cooked preparation unstated; Nguni people claim mild laxative effects.",
    "evidence": {
      "summary": ["s1:p2", "s1:p3", "s1:p6", "s1:p25"],
      "humanEdibility": ["s1:p20", "s1:p25"]
    }
  },
