    "taxonId": 119546,
    "summary": "A hairy perennial shrub from the fynbos of the Cape Peninsula and nearby southwestern Cape, wild mallow grows upright from an underground rootstock and becomes woody at the base. Its crowded, sometimes hood-shaped leaves are fragrant when rubbed, and its flowers range from white to purplish red.",
    "humanEdibility": "unknown",
    "edibilityNote": null,
