  {
    "taxonId": 336806,
    "summary": "A succulent flowering plant endemic to the Canary Islands, the candle-plant has jointed branches resembling rows of sausages. Thick elongated leaves cluster at branch tips and fall at the start of the dry season, while fragrant grey-white flowers may appear from March through October.",
    "humanEdibility": "unknown",
    "edibilityNote": null,
    "evidence": {
